<title>SRI LANKA: Tea Smallholder up on retail buying.</title>
<headline>Tea Smallholder up on retail buying.</headline>
<dateline>COLOMBO 1996-09-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Tea Smallholder Factories Ltd rose 2.94 percent, or 50 cents, to 17.50 on buying of 12,000 shares by retail investors, brokers said.</p>
<p>&quot;High tea prices and overall good performance by plantations have increased demand for stocks in the tea business,&quot; said a local broker.</p>
<p>The company processes tea bought from small-scale tea cultivators.</p>
<p>--Colombo newsroom (941) 434319</p>
</text>
